# beam4pm-mcp-contracts-pack vocabulary.
#
# Mirrors beam4pm-ai-contracts-pack's aic:ContractType / aic:Field pattern
# (itself mirroring beam4pm-process-model-pack's bpm:RecordType / bpm:Field
# pattern) exactly, under a sibling namespace and prefix, for a sibling
# domain: the canonical MCP (Model Context Protocol) wire-message data
# shapes -- the JSON-RPC 2.0 envelope (request, success response, error
# response, notification) and the tools/resources message payloads (tool,
# tool-call request/result, resource, resource-read request/result).
#
# Verified against the real MCP specification, fetched and read directly:
# https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/
# All ten message shapes below use the spec's own field names verbatim
# (jsonrpc, id, method, params, result, error {code, message, data} as ONE
# wrapped object -- see the rpc_error_response note below, name, title,
# description, inputSchema/outputSchema -> input_schema/output_schema in
# this snake_case vocabulary (see mcp:wireName below), arguments, content,
# isError -> is_error, structuredContent -> structured_content, uri,
# mimeType -> mime_type, size, contents) -- none were invented.
#
# Consumer message-type individuals (the ten admitted mcp:MessageType
# instances) are NOT declared here -- per this marketplace's established
# contract, packs' *instance data* is supplied by the consuming project's
# own ontology.ttl (e.g. beam4pm), built from this vocabulary. This file
# contains ZERO individuals. (This pack DOES ship real templates -- see
# templates/ and README.md's "What this pack generates" -- only the ten
# admitted mcp:MessageType/mcp:Field individuals themselves are consumer-
# supplied, the same division every sibling beam4pm-*-contracts-pack uses.)
#
# Scope boundary (deliberate, not an oversight): this vocabulary models wire-
# message data shapes only. It carries no tool-execution, transport,
# session, or capability-negotiation semantics of any kind. In particular:
#   - A JSON-RPC id is real-spec `string | number`; this vocabulary models it
#     as a single "string" field. Numeric ids are expected to be stringified
#     by callers before constructing a message -- a real, bounded
#     compression, not a silent narrowing, and it is disclosed in README.md.
#   - `tools/call`'s result `content` (an array of typed content blocks, each
#     discriminated by a `type` tag: text/image/audio/resource_link/
#     resource/...) and `resources/read`'s result `contents` (an array of
#     `{uri, mimeType?, text?}` or `{uri, mimeType?, blob?}` items) are each
#     modeled as ONE "map" field wrapping the real array under a single key
#     (e.g. `{"blocks": [...]}` / `{"contents": [...]}`). The closed 8-value
#     fieldType enum below has no "array of typed objects" member, so the
#     wrapped array's own elements are not independently field-validated by
#     this pack -- a real, bounded scope limit disclosed in README.md, not a
#     defect. A future revision of this pack could model content-block types
#     as their own mcp:MessageType if a real consumer needs field-level
#     validation on them.
#   - `rpc_error_response`'s real-spec `error` value is ONE nested object
#     (`{"code": ..., "message": ..., "data": ...}`), per JSON-RPC 2.0 and
#     the MCP schema's own `JSONRPCError` definition. This vocabulary models
#     it the same "wrap the whole object as one map field" way as `content`/
#     `contents` above: a single `error`:`map` field, not three flattened
#     `error_code`/`error_message`/`error_data` fields. Flattening would be a
#     real, undisclosed wire-breaking divergence (no real MCP peer sends or
#     understands top-level `error_code`/`error_message` keys) -- disclosed
#     in README.md, not silently modeled that way.
#   - Five fields have a real MCP wire-format JSON key that differs from
#     this vocabulary's own snake_case `mcp:fieldName` (the Erlang atom /
#     Elixir struct field identifier): `inputSchema`, `outputSchema`,
#     `isError`, `structuredContent`, `mimeType`. The OPTIONAL `mcp:wireName`
#     property below (falls back to `mcp:fieldName` when absent) carries the
#     real wire spelling for exactly those five fields, so generated codecs
#     emit/read the real JSON key while the Erlang/Elixir-side identifier
#     stays snake_case -- disclosed in README.md, not a silent renaming.
#   - Authority, admission, replay, and refusal semantics of any kind are
#     entirely out of scope for this vocabulary; they are the exclusive,
#     separately-owned responsibility of beam4pm-post-llm-runtime-pack's
#     rt: vocabulary. This pack neither touches nor extends that vocabulary.

@prefix mcp: <https://ggen.dev/ontology/beam4pm-mcp#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

mcp:MessageType a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Message Type" ;
    rdfs:comment "One admitted MCP wire-message data shape (JSON-RPC request, success response, error response, notification, tool, tool-call request/result, resource, or resource-read request/result) projected into generated code." .

mcp:Field a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field" ;
    rdfs:comment "One typed, ordered field belonging to an mcp:MessageType." .

mcp:messageName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:MessageType ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "The message type's canonical snake_case name (e.g. rpc_request)." .
mcp:messageDoc a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:MessageType ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
mcp:hasField a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:MessageType ; rdfs:range mcp:Field .
mcp:fieldName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
mcp:fieldType a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Closed set: string, integer, float, boolean, datetime, atom, list_string, map." .
mcp:fieldDoc a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
mcp:fieldRequired a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Plain string literal true or false; templates compare it as a string." .
mcp:fieldOrder a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:integer .
mcp:wireName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain mcp:Field ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "OPTIONAL. The field's real MCP wire-format JSON key, when it differs from mcp:fieldName (e.g. camelCase inputSchema vs. this vocabulary's snake_case field_name input_schema). Every template that emits or reads a JSON key selects COALESCE(wireName, fieldName) for that key; mcp:fieldName alone remains the Erlang atom / Elixir struct field identifier and never changes. Set explicitly only on the five fields with a real camelCase wire spelling: inputSchema, outputSchema, isError, structuredContent, mimeType." .
